  "body": "**Link to problem area**: https://spec.matrix.org/v1.3/client-server-api/#mroommember\r\n\r\n**Issue**\r\nThere was [this spec clarification](https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec-proposals/pull/3730) that says that `invite -> knock` is allowed according to the auth rules.\r\n\r\nNow I look at the [auth rules](https://spec.matrix.org/unstable/rooms/v10/#authorization-rules) (rule 5.7.3) and I get this reconstituted sentence if I pick the correct parts:\r\n\r\n> If (the new) membership is `knock` and if the current membership is **not** `invite`, allow.\r\n\r\nWhich means `invite -> knock` should be rejected.\r\n\r\n**Expected behaviour**\r\nThis part of the clarification should be reverted with this action not allowed, like before.\r\n",
